Graph Terminologies :
---------------------

Graph = Nodes + Edges

1. undirected graph
2. undirected cyclic graph
3. directed graph
4. directed cyclic graph
5. directed acyclic graph (DAG)

Path = contains a lot of nodes and each of them are reachable

NOTE : a node cannot appear twice in a path !!

Degree of a Node = number of edges attached to it (Undirected graph)

NOTE : sum of all degrees of nodes = 2 * total number of edges (Undirected graph)

Indegree of a Node = number of incoming edges from a node (Directed graph)

Outdegree of a Node = number of outgoing edges from a node (Directed graph)

Weighted edge = an edge assigned a specific numerical value, known as a weight or cost

