How to Store graph in Java : (directed and undirected both)
----------------------------

1. Adjacency Matrix
2. Adjacency List

lets consider 1-based indexing graph :

- Adjacency Matrix graph = Integer[n+1][n+1], n = number of nodes
  here, graph[i][j] = 1, => there is edge from i to j (i -> j)
        graph[i][j] = 0, => no edge from i to j

  in weighted graph, graph[i][j] contains the weight from i -> j

NOTE : space complexity = O(n^2)

- Adjacency List graph = ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> graph;
  here, i -> x, where x belongs to graph.get(i) list

  in weighted graph => ArrayList<ArrayList<Pair<Integer, Integer>>> graph;

NOTE : space complexity = O(V+E) but in a sparse graph, i.e. E << V^2
       Thus, we always use adjacency list representation of graph

